<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Arduino on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/arduino/</link><description>Recent content in Arduino on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 29 Jan 2015 12:47:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/arduino/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Arduino LCD Matrix 3x5 Numeric Font Test</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-lcd-matrix-3x5-numeric-font-test/</link><pubDate>Thu, 29 Jan 2015 12:47:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-lcd-matrix-3x5-numeric-font-test/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Minimal 3x5 numeric font on a LCD Matrix for Arduino Nano.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/-U3vCb16cW8" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe allowtransparency="true" frameborder="0" src="https://codebender.cc/embed/sketch:78905" style="height: 510px; margin: 10px 0 10px; width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>LED Matrix Arduino Nano</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/led-matrix-arduino-nano/</link><pubDate>Wed, 28 Jan 2015 08:42:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/led-matrix-arduino-nano/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe allowfullscreen="" frameborder="0" height="270" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/IYBRyIQGTh0" width="480"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Testing a LCD Max7219 Matrix with an Arduino Nano, thank to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="http://tronixstuff.com/2013/10/11/tutorial-arduino-max7219-led-display-driver-ic/" target="_blank"&gt;http://tronixstuff.com/2013/10/11/tutorial-arduino-max7219-led-display-driver-ic/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;#include&amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;LedControl&lt;/span&gt;.h&amp;gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;LedControl&lt;/span&gt; lc=&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;LedControl&lt;/span&gt;(12,11,10,1);&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// pin 12 is connected to the MAX7219 pin 1&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// pin 11 is connected to the CLK pin 13&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// pin 10 is connected to LOAD pin 12&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// 1 as we are only using 1 MAX7219&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;(){&#10;  lc.&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;shutdown&lt;/span&gt;(0,&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;  lc.&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;setIntensity&lt;/span&gt;(0,8);&#10;  lc.&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;clearDisplay&lt;/span&gt;(0);&#10;}&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Arduino Uno Serial Message Project at Code Bender</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-uno-serial-message-project-at/</link><pubDate>Wed, 26 Mar 2014 14:08:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-uno-serial-message-project-at/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/13426924513" title="Codebender by Alastair Montgomery, on Flickr"&gt;&lt;img src="https://farm8.staticflickr.com/7060/13426924513_92097b40dc.jpg" width="500" height="486" alt="Codebender"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Project to send scrolling messages to LCD Shield enabled Arduino Uno at Codebender.&#10;Codebender lets you code and program your Arduino from a browser.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe style="height: 510px; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0 10px;" allowTransparency="true" src="https://codebender.cc/embed/sketch:32460" frameborder="0"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#10;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;</description></item><item><title>Day 169 Light holiday reading</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/day-169-light-holiday-reading/</link><pubDate>Thu, 12 Sep 2013 14:26:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/day-169-light-holiday-reading/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; the only link in this post is now broken. Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'&gt;&lt;img style='max-width:586px;' src='http://farm8.staticflickr.com/7289/9732431638_e1d213ac15_b.jpg'/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;New Arduino book :) http://flic.kr/p/fQ2fRu, September 12, 2013 at 04:11PM&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>123D Circuits</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/123d-circuits/</link><pubDate>Thu, 12 Sep 2013 14:13:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/123d-circuits/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Been trying out &lt;a href="http://123d.circuits.io/" target="_blank"&gt;123D Circuits&lt;/a&gt; an GITHUB style online circuit designer and simulator.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe frameborder="0" height="448" marginheight="0" marginwidth="0" scrolling="no" src="http://123d.circuits.io/circuits/28975/embed" width="725"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Ruby Script to send Twitter mentions over serial port</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/ruby-script-to-send-twitter-mentions/</link><pubDate>Tue, 19 Mar 2013 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/ruby-script-to-send-twitter-mentions/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Short script to send Twitter mention messages to a serial port using Ruby and the gems twitter and serialport.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;# Find your Twitter Mentions and send them to Arduino on Serial Port&#10;&lt;p&gt;require &amp;ldquo;rubygems&amp;rdquo;&#10;require &amp;ldquo;twitter&amp;rdquo; #https://github.com/sferik/twitter for config details&#10;require &amp;ldquo;serialport&amp;rdquo; #http://rubygems.org/gems/serialport&#10;require &amp;ldquo;pp&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;prevID = 0&#10;puts &amp;ldquo;Setting Up Serial Port&amp;rdquo;&#10;myport = SerialPort.new(&amp;quot;/dev/ttyACM0&amp;quot;,&amp;ldquo;9600&amp;rdquo;.to_i)&#10;sleep(10)&#10;while true&#10;puts &amp;ldquo;Checking for mentions&amp;rdquo;&#10;latestMention = Twitter.mentions(:count =&amp;gt; 1)[0]&#10;if prevID != latestMention.id&#10;msg = latestMention.user.screen_name + &amp;quot; &amp;quot; + latestMention.text&#10;puts &amp;ldquo;-&amp;rdquo; + msg&#10;bytes = myport.write(msg)&#10;puts &amp;ldquo;-&amp;rdquo; + bytes.to_s&#10;prevID = latestMention.id&#10;else&#10;puts &amp;ldquo;-No new updates&amp;rdquo;&#10;end&#10;sleep 60&#10;end&#10;myport.close&#10;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Arduino LCD Message Scroller working</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-lcd-message-scroller-working/</link><pubDate>Tue, 19 Mar 2013 10:13:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-lcd-message-scroller-working/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Got my Arduino LCD message scroller working last night, will post a video later when I do an end to end test with my Twitter mentions.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;object width="320" height="266" class="BLOGGER-youtube-video" classid="clsid:D27CDB6E-AE6D-11cf-96B8-444553540000" codebase="http://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=6,0,40,0" data-thumbnail-src="https://ytimg.googleusercontent.com/vi/g2Ql86wt8dI/0.jpg"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="https://www.youtube.com/v/g2Ql86wt8dI?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" /&gt;&lt;param name="bgcolor" value="#FFFFFF" /&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true" /&gt;&lt;embed width="320" height="266" src="https://www.youtube.com/v/g2Ql86wt8dI?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Here is the code (also at GitHub &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/arduino.git"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/arduino.git&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;//&amp;nbsp;Auto&amp;nbsp;scroll&amp;nbsp;a&amp;nbsp;message&amp;nbsp;on&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;LCD&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;receive&amp;nbsp;new&amp;nbsp;messages&amp;nbsp;via&amp;nbsp;Serial&amp;nbsp;port.&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;//&amp;nbsp;Alastair&amp;nbsp;Montgomery&amp;nbsp;(c)&amp;nbsp;2013&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;//&amp;nbsp;Version&amp;nbsp;1.02&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&amp;nbsp;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;//&amp;nbsp;include&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;library&amp;nbsp;code:&lt;/span&gt;&#10;#include&amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;LiquidCrystal&lt;/span&gt;.h&amp;gt;&#10;#include&amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;string.h&amp;gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// initialize the library with the numbers of the interface pins&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// below for SainSmart LCD Shield&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;LiquidCrystal&lt;/span&gt; lcd(8, 9, 4, 5, 6, 7);&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Some Debug Required</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/some-debug-required/</link><pubDate>Sun, 17 Mar 2013 21:51:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/some-debug-required/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;First test of Twitter updates getting written to the Arduino from Ruby didn't go quite right as seen from the video below, some debugging required.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Testing writing the same message from the Arduino IDE gives the same results so looks like problem is in the Arduino code. Maybe the message is too long for the LCD's buffer?&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;object class="BLOGGER-youtube-video" classid="clsid:D27CDB6E-AE6D-11cf-96B8-444553540000" codebase="http://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=6,0,40,0" data-thumbnail-src="http://i.ytimg.com/vi/g2Ql86wt8dI/0.jpg" height="266" width="320"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/g2Ql86wt8dI?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" /&gt;&lt;param name="bgcolor" value="#FFFFFF" /&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true" /&gt;&lt;embed width="320" height="266" src="http://www.youtube.com/v/g2Ql86wt8dI?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;The Twitter to Serial port Ruby script can be found at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/arduino/tree/master/SerialMessage"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/arduino/tree/master/SerialMessage&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sending Arduino messages over serial port</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/sending-arduino-messages-over-serial/</link><pubDate>Thu, 14 Mar 2013 08:52:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/sending-arduino-messages-over-serial/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 6 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="text-align: left;"&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="background-color: white;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #333333; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;Video of sending a message to the Arduino over the serial port which then gets scrolled on a SainSmart LCD shield.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="background-color: white; color: #333333; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="background-color: white; color: #333333; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;Idea was to use it to display tweets, just need to write the Ruby code to get the tweet and send it over the serial port now.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="background-color: white; color: #333333; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;object class="BLOGGER-youtube-video" classid="clsid:D27CDB6E-AE6D-11cf-96B8-444553540000" codebase="http://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=6,0,40,0" data-thumbnail-src="http://i.ytimg.com/vi/1xrbyvgB7L0/0.jpg" height="266" width="320"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/1xrbyvgB7L0?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" /&gt;&lt;param name="bgcolor" value="#FFFFFF" /&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true" /&gt;&lt;embed width="320" height="266" src="http://www.youtube.com/v/1xrbyvgB7L0?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="background-color: white; color: #333333; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="background-color: white; color: #333333; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="background-color: white; color: #333333; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;Here is the first version of the sketch uploaded to the Arduino.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="background-color: white; color: #333333; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;All code can be found at&lt;a href="http://www.blogger.com/goog_1929310187"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: #333333; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: x-small;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 17px;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/arduino.git"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/arduino.git&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="background-color: white; color: #333333; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="background-color: white; color: #333333; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="background-color: #f6f6f6; color: #333333; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="background-color: #f6f6f6; color: #333333; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;//&amp;nbsp;Auto&amp;nbsp;scroll&amp;nbsp;a&amp;nbsp;message&amp;nbsp;on&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;LCD&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;receive&amp;nbsp;new&amp;nbsp;messages&amp;nbsp;via&amp;nbsp;Serial&amp;nbsp;port.&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;//&amp;nbsp;Alastair&amp;nbsp;Montgomery&amp;nbsp;(c)&amp;nbsp;2013&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;//&amp;nbsp;Version&amp;nbsp;1.00&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&amp;nbsp;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;//&amp;nbsp;include&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;library&amp;nbsp;code:&lt;/span&gt;&#10;#include&amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;LiquidCrystal&lt;/span&gt;.h&amp;gt;&#10;#include&amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;string.h&amp;gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// initialize the library with the numbers of the interface pins&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// below for SainSmart LCD Shield&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;LiquidCrystal&lt;/span&gt; lcd(8, 9, 4, 5, 6, 7);&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sainsmart LCD Shield Test</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/sainsmart-lcd-shield-test/</link><pubDate>Wed, 06 Mar 2013 22:35:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/sainsmart-lcd-shield-test/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Testing my Sainsmart LCD Shield.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;object width="320" height="266" class="BLOGGER-youtube-video" classid="clsid:D27CDB6E-AE6D-11cf-96B8-444553540000" codebase="http://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=6,0,40,0" data-thumbnail-src="http://i.ytimg.com/vi/xx7y3yGC76A/0.jpg"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/xx7y3yGC76A?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" /&gt;&lt;param name="bgcolor" value="#FFFFFF" /&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true" /&gt;&lt;embed width="320" height="266" src="http://www.youtube.com/v/xx7y3yGC76A?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;/*&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;LiquidCrystal&amp;nbsp;Library&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;Hello&amp;nbsp;World&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Demonstrates&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;use&amp;nbsp;a&amp;nbsp;16x2&amp;nbsp;LCD&amp;nbsp;display.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;The&amp;nbsp;LiquidCrystal&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;library&amp;nbsp;works&amp;nbsp;with&amp;nbsp;all&amp;nbsp;LCD&amp;nbsp;displays&amp;nbsp;that&amp;nbsp;are&amp;nbsp;compatible&amp;nbsp;with&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Hitachi&amp;nbsp;HD44780&amp;nbsp;driver.&amp;nbsp;There&amp;nbsp;are&amp;nbsp;many&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;them&amp;nbsp;out&amp;nbsp;there,&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;you&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;can&amp;nbsp;usually&amp;nbsp;tell&amp;nbsp;them&amp;nbsp;by&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;16-pin&amp;nbsp;interface.&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;This&amp;nbsp;sketch&amp;nbsp;prints&amp;nbsp;"Hello&amp;nbsp;World!"&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;LCD&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;shows&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;time.&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;The&amp;nbsp;circuit:&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;*&amp;nbsp;LCD&amp;nbsp;RS&amp;nbsp;pin&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;digital&amp;nbsp;pin&amp;nbsp;12&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;*&amp;nbsp;LCD&amp;nbsp;Enable&amp;nbsp;pin&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;digital&amp;nbsp;pin&amp;nbsp;11&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;*&amp;nbsp;LCD&amp;nbsp;D4&amp;nbsp;pin&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;digital&amp;nbsp;pin&amp;nbsp;5&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;*&amp;nbsp;LCD&amp;nbsp;D5&amp;nbsp;pin&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;digital&amp;nbsp;pin&amp;nbsp;4&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;*&amp;nbsp;LCD&amp;nbsp;D6&amp;nbsp;pin&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;digital&amp;nbsp;pin&amp;nbsp;3&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;*&amp;nbsp;LCD&amp;nbsp;D7&amp;nbsp;pin&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;digital&amp;nbsp;pin&amp;nbsp;2&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;*&amp;nbsp;LCD&amp;nbsp;R/W&amp;nbsp;pin&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;ground&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;*&amp;nbsp;10K&amp;nbsp;resistor:&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;*&amp;nbsp;ends&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;+5V&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;ground&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;*&amp;nbsp;wiper&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;LCD&amp;nbsp;VO&amp;nbsp;pin&amp;nbsp;(pin&amp;nbsp;3)&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Library&amp;nbsp;originally&amp;nbsp;added&amp;nbsp;18&amp;nbsp;Apr&amp;nbsp;2008&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;by&amp;nbsp;David&amp;nbsp;A.&amp;nbsp;Mellis&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;library&amp;nbsp;modified&amp;nbsp;5&amp;nbsp;Jul&amp;nbsp;2009&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;by&amp;nbsp;Limor&amp;nbsp;Fried&amp;nbsp;(http://www.ladyada.net)&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;example&amp;nbsp;added&amp;nbsp;9&amp;nbsp;Jul&amp;nbsp;2009&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;by&amp;nbsp;Tom&amp;nbsp;Igoe&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;modified&amp;nbsp;22&amp;nbsp;Nov&amp;nbsp;2010&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;by&amp;nbsp;Tom&amp;nbsp;Igoe&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;This&amp;nbsp;example&amp;nbsp;code&amp;nbsp;is&amp;nbsp;in&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;public&amp;nbsp;domain.&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt; http://www.arduino.cc/en/Tutorial/LiquidCrystal&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt; */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// include the library code:&lt;/span&gt;&#10;#include &amp;lt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;LiquidCrystal&lt;/span&gt;.h&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// initialize the library with the numbers of the interface pins&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;//LiquidCrystal lcd(12, 11, 5, 4, 3, 2);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;LiquidCrystal&lt;/span&gt; lcd(8, 9, 4, 5, 6, 7);&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>LCD shield</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/lcd-shield/</link><pubDate>Sat, 05 Jan 2013 15:25:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/lcd-shield/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Latest toy for my Arduino, now what to use it for?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class='separator' style='clear: both; text-align: center;'&gt; &lt;a href='https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgZm3wE508LFiLKRnRW-BIu4DARKW2KtKY_6i6WdRoj03V_Bd592XBUe26bS0QNO1Vi-AYzbRvWKuXBodhpX2hZGhh5_kEStIdNAsqw08NdzPJl7RuSCxS0MPDSHqXS-dWziQHhg6p4prc/s1600/camera_Hagrid_Burn_Cornered.jpg' imageanchor='1' style='margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;'&gt; &lt;img border='0' src='https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgZm3wE508LFiLKRnRW-BIu4DARKW2KtKY_6i6WdRoj03V_Bd592XBUe26bS0QNO1Vi-AYzbRvWKuXBodhpX2hZGhh5_kEStIdNAsqw08NdzPJl7RuSCxS0MPDSHqXS-dWziQHhg6p4prc/s640/camera_Hagrid_Burn_Cornered.jpg' /&gt; &lt;/a&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Arduino Code on Github</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-code-on-github/</link><pubDate>Thu, 06 Dec 2012 13:07:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-code-on-github/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;I've started uploading my Arduino examples code to Github&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/arduino"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/arduino&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Counting up to 1023</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/counting-up-to-1023/</link><pubDate>Sun, 25 Nov 2012 22:03:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/counting-up-to-1023/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Decided in the end to wire up all 10 LEDS in the LED bar graph.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Using the sketch below get the results shown in the video.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;object class="BLOGGER-youtube-video" classid="clsid:D27CDB6E-AE6D-11cf-96B8-444553540000" codebase="http://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=6,0,40,0" data-thumbnail-src="https://ytimg.googleusercontent.com/vi/1TVgph8aZE4/0.jpg" height="266" width="320"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="https://www.youtube.com/v/1TVgph8aZE4?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" /&gt;&lt;param name="bgcolor" value="#FFFFFF" /&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true" /&gt;&lt;embed width="320" height="266" src="https://www.youtube.com/v/1TVgph8aZE4?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; numLed = 10;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; ledpins[] = {&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;13,12,11,10,9,8,7,6,5,4};&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; mask[] = {&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512};&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; counter = 0;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;() { &lt;br&gt;&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// initialize the digital pin as an output.&lt;/span&gt;&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; i=0;i&amp;lt;numLed;i++){&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;pinMode&lt;/span&gt;(ledpins[i], &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;digitalWrite&lt;/span&gt;(ledpins[i], &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;HIGH&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;(250);&#10;  }&#10;}&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Arduino Binary second counter</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-binary-second-counter/</link><pubDate>Fri, 23 Nov 2012 14:46:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-binary-second-counter/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Next step with my Arduino is to set up a binary second counter.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Basic using the LED Bar Graph or six single LEDs to count seconds in binary&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjNmgs8Izk2utl30ZAVCskDyYVZ2wMyj97vYfOIO-uxLJk1cOgJ_ZaY-_LZmbyjDATFZWzCzKZQVxI7P1Y1obG7oL9eIb0x5no0MF79yfG4KTp3ruXU9Xn-ZY-ZUMVihaNaLlNvoxhBcW8/s1600/six+leds_bb.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="290" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjNmgs8Izk2utl30ZAVCskDyYVZ2wMyj97vYfOIO-uxLJk1cOgJ_ZaY-_LZmbyjDATFZWzCzKZQVxI7P1Y1obG7oL9eIb0x5no0MF79yfG4KTp3ruXU9Xn-ZY-ZUMVihaNaLlNvoxhBcW8/s320/six+leds_bb.png" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;/*&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;Binary&amp;nbsp;Second&amp;nbsp;Counter&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Created&amp;nbsp;Alastair&amp;nbsp;Montgomery&amp;nbsp;22/11/2012&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;*/&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; ledPins[] = {&#10;  7,8,9,10,11,12};&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; mask[] = {&#10;  1,2,4,8,16,32};&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; ledCount = 6;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;() {&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; thisPin =0; thisPin &amp;lt; ledCount; thisPin++) {&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;pinMode&lt;/span&gt;(ledPins[thisPin], &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;  }&#10;}&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sanity Checking my new Arduino Uno Board</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/sanity-checking-my-new-arduino-uno-board/</link><pubDate>Thu, 22 Nov 2012 22:13:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/sanity-checking-my-new-arduino-uno-board/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Quick sanity check of my new Arduino board using a LED Bar Graph.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;object width="320" height="266" class="BLOGGER-youtube-video" classid="clsid:D27CDB6E-AE6D-11cf-96B8-444553540000" codebase="http://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=6,0,40,0" data-thumbnail-src="https://ytimg.googleusercontent.com/vi/L7ri5PBrsQU/0.jpg"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="https://www.youtube.com/v/L7ri5PBrsQU?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" /&gt;&lt;param name="bgcolor" value="#FFFFFF" /&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true" /&gt;&lt;embed width="320" height="266" src="https://www.youtube.com/v/L7ri5PBrsQU?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Here is the sketch I will be using.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; led1 = 8;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; led2 = 9;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; counter = 0;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;() { &lt;br&gt;&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// initialize the digital pin as an output.&lt;/span&gt;&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;pinMode&lt;/span&gt;(led1, &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;pinMode&lt;/span&gt;(led2, &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/span&gt;);&lt;br&gt;&#10;}&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;loop&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;() {&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (counter &amp;amp; 1) {&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;digitalWrite&lt;/span&gt;(led1, &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;HIGH&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;  }&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; {&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;digitalWrite&lt;/span&gt;(led1, &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;LOW&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;  }&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>